{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py:638` computes `_sev = severity_label(imp)` and discards it (\"keep the call so severity_label stays exercised\"); `severity_label` at `:621` is already exercised by `tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py:72-76` and `tests/unit/test_divergence_grade_split.py:104`. `src/rebar/llm/workflow/steps.py:202,208,214,242` still fail the `gate` step on `fail_on_severity` beside the ADR-0108 `priority_threshold` (`:204,210,216,244`); ADR 0108 `:131-136` records this as an unwired sample-only policy, and `fail_on_severity` exists nowhere else (no config key, no `_config_schema.py` entry, no mechanism-baseline row). `src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_verdict.schema.json:5` says findings carry `severity`; `src/rebar/schemas/gate_input.schema.json:10` says each finding \"is an object with a `severity`\". `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_ops.py:193-208` reads `REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH` (`:198`, `# read-via: subsystem-kill-switch`) for the story-a9dd A/B, which is finished; the default (unset) path is the `else` branch `:201-208` (prefetch ON). Operator rulings: remove both, with release notes. Cites re-measured on ee5253abfd4.\n\n## Approach\n1. `decide.py`: delete the discarded `_sev = severity_label(imp)` at `:638`.\n2. `steps.py`: delete the three `\"fail_on_severity\"` keys and `:242` (`if finding.get(\"severity\") in policy[\"fail_on_severity\"]: return True`); rewrite the comment at `:195-198` (\"fails when any finding's `priority` is at or above the policy's `priority_threshold` or the count exceeds `max_findings`\"). `advisory` keeps `priority_threshold: None`.\n3. `gate_input.schema.json:10` becomes \"each item is an object with a `priority`\" — that schema describes the WORKFLOW `gate` step's input, which is exactly what stops keying on severity. **`plan_review_verdict.schema.json:5` is left UNCHANGED.** Its `severity` is a different, still-authored field: plan-review findings emit it live (a deterministic P6 finding carries `\"severity\": \"minor\"`), and it is unrelated to the gate-step `fail_on_severity` and the `review_kernel` `_sev` this story removes. Stripping it would stop documenting a key the surface still produces. Neither edited string is in the generated `types.py` subset; `python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types --check` proves it.\n4. `gate_ops.py`: delete `:193-201` (comment, `import os`, the `if` and its two lines) and the `else:`, dedenting `:202-208`; keep the `prefetch_manifest` name.\n5. Generated artifacts, regenerated not hand-edited. `docs/env-vars.md:147` disappears via `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py`. `.github/mechanism-baseline.json:582` holds `\"env_var::REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH\": 1`; removing the read makes it `stale`, which the shrink-only ratchet ALLOWS, and AGENTS.md directs a change that removes a mechanism to run `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` and commit the shrunken baseline. **There is no `tests/scripts/test_llm_seam_clean_heldout.py` and no `_TOTAL_MARKER_CAP` anywhere in the tree** — an earlier draft named both; the marker this step retires is the `# read-via: subsystem-kill-switch` comment on `gate_ops.py:198`, and the ratchet above is what actually tracks it.\n6. `docs/release-notes.md`: \"`REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH` removed: the completion verifier's file-impact prefetch is always on (the a9dd A/B is finished). The sample `gate` workflow step no longer fails on `severity`; policies key on `priority_threshold` only (ADR 0108).\"\n\n## Scope\nThe files above. `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` is in scope as a REGENERATED artifact (`--update-stale`), never hand-edited. Out of scope: `findings.py` `SEVERITIES` vocabulary (ADR 0108 amendment 3), the `completion_*` severity consumers, `severity_label` itself, and `plan_review_verdict.schema.json`.\n\n## Testing\n`tests/unit/workflow/test_steps.py:29,35,40,46` (severity-driven cases): rewrite to `priority`-driven equivalents (`{\"priority\": 0.99}` fails default; strict via `max_findings`; advisory never fails; unknown policy falls back), keep `:56-91`. `tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py:78-97` unchanged (asserts no `severity` key, still true). Prefetch tests: `tests/unit/test_ticket_description_limit.py:216` and `tests/unit/workflow/test_child_closure_evidence_6ec8.py:45` replace `monkeypatch.setenv(\"REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH\", \"0\")` with `monkeypatch.setattr(\"rebar.llm.workflow.completion_prefetch.assemble_prefetch\", lambda spec, *, repo_root: (\"\", []))` (the idiom at `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_prefetch.py:199-202`; `fit_within_ceiling(base, \"\", model)` returns `\"\"` so context equals base). Add `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_prefetch.py::test_precheck_always_prefetches` (spy `assemble_prefetch` called once with `PrefetchSpec(ticket_id, graph)`; both `monkeypatch.delenv(\"REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH\", raising=False)` and `setenv(..., \"0\")` still call it).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `git grep -n \"fail_on_severity\\|REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH\\|severity_label(imp)\" -- src tests docs scripts .github ':!docs/adr' ':!docs/release-notes.md' ':!.github/mechanism-baseline.json'` prints nothing.\n- [x] `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py && git diff --exit-code docs/env-vars.md` is clean and the file has no `REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH` row.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` reports `new=0` with `REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH` listed under stale.\n- [x] `git grep -n 'read-via: subsystem-kill-switch' -- src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_ops.py` prints nothing, and the two surviving marker sites (`_mcp_inflight.py`, `gate_context.py`) are untouched.\n- [x] `plan_review_verdict.schema.json` still lists `severity` among finding keys: `grep -c 'severity' src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_verdict.schema.json` is non-zero, proving the live plan-review field was not stripped with the gate-step one.\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793164289582879106,"uuid":"bd31cff3-9221-4de5-bc1c-8507f94df14e"}